.env*
!.env.example
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
/attesttag
bot.log

# Private keys, certificates and credential files. The GitHub App setup hands the operator a
# .pem, and none of these should ever be sweep-able into a commit by `git add .`.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*credentials*.json
*service-account*.json

ui/node_modules
ui/.next
# The console build, except the one placeholder //go:embed needs to compile (ui/embed.go).
ui/out/*
!ui/out/index.html

# macOS finder metadata
.DS_Store
# Claude Code local session state and worktrees
.claude/

# Per-organisation document storage (DOCS_DIR default is ./docs). The seed documents at the
# root are checked in; everything under docs/org-<id>/ is a tenant's own uploaded files.
docs/org-*/

# Not code, and nothing a self-hoster needs to build or run the service: the walkthrough
# recorder (video/), the logo explorations and the Slack Marketplace screenshots with their
# generator. They stay on the maintainers' disks. This repository is public, so what it holds
# is the source and what building it needs — see the pre-push check in .githooks/.
video/
assets/icon-options/
assets/marketplace/
assets/attest-tag-icon.png
*.mp4

# The security audits (security-review/). A report is a map of the attack surface with working
# reproductions in it, and two earlier ones reached the history before this line existed — which
# is why publishing means a fresh repository rather than this one. Never commit another.
security-review/

# Python bytecode from deploy/test's fake cloud CLIs.
__pycache__/
strix_runs/
